      <miscellaneous-field name="analysis-json">{"meta":{"id":"chopin_op28_funeral_march","parent_item_id":"chopin_op28_funeral_march","title":"Prelude: Op. 28, No. 20","composer":"Frédéric Chopin","source_file":"files/scores/chopin_op28_funeral_march.mid","quarter_range":[0,52.0],"bar_quarters":4.0,"time_signature":"4/4","key":"c","tempo":42.0,"midi_play_url":"files/scores/chopin_op28_funeral_march.mid","source_licence":"PD","notation_notes":"Mutopia MIDI (PD edition, piece 472): 13 bars of 4/4, no pickup, quarter range 0–52, quarter = 42 throughout. Bars 9–12 are written out (the printed repeat of bars 5–8); not doubled. Beat 3 of most bars is a dotted-eighth + sixteenth figure. Constant MIDI velocity: printed ff / p / pp and the crescendo in bar 12 are not in the source and are not inferred. Ab/Db/Gb sound as G#/C#/F# spellings in the MIDI-derived score. MIDI-derived score, not an Urtext.","source_page":"https://www.mutopiaproject.org/cgibin/piece-info.cgi?id=472","suggested_arrangement_tempo":42,"sustain_events":[{"quarter":0.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":1.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":1.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":2.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":2.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":3.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":3.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":4.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":4.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":5.0,"channel":1,"value":0},{"quarter":47.0,"channel":1,"value":127},{"quarter":48.0,"channel":1,"value":0}]},"draft":false,"reviewed_by":"claude-opus-5-5 (MusicBot) 2026-10-11","summary":"C minor throughout. Thirteen bars of block chords, one per beat. Phrase 1 (1–4) states the march: i–iv7–V7–i, a one-bar visit to Ab (VI, with Db), then C7→Fm and V/V→V, ending on a half cadence. Phrase 2 (5–8) moves the melody up an octave over a chromatic bass (C down to Eb) that passes a French sixth, then cadences: V65→i (bar 7) and the Neapolitan Db→V7→i PAC (bar 8). Bars 9–12 repeat 5–8 exactly; bar 13 is a held tonic chord.","sections":[{"name":"A (march)","start_bar":1,"end_bar":4,"mood":["solemn","grave","heavy"],"description":"Full chords with octave bass; i–iv7–V7–i, Ab tonicized in bar 2, HC on G in bar 4."},{"name":"B (lament)","start_bar":5,"end_bar":8,"mood":["mournful","tender"],"description":"Higher melody over a semitone-by-semitone falling bass; French sixth (bar 6), IAC (bar 7), Neapolitan → PAC (bar 8)."},{"name":"B′ (echo)","start_bar":9,"end_bar":12,"mood":["mournful","hushed"],"description":"Exact repeat of bars 5–8 (printed pp; dynamics not in the MIDI)."},{"name":"Coda","start_bar":13,"end_bar":13,"mood":["final","still"],"description":"Held C-minor chord."}],"mood":[{"start_bar":1,"end_bar":4,"labels":["solemn","grave","heavy"]},{"start_bar":5,"end_bar":8,"labels":["mournful","tender"]},{"start_bar":9,"end_bar":12,"labels":["mournful","hushed"]},{"start_bar":13,"end_bar":13,"labels":["final","still"]}],"tricks":["Every beat is a new full chord: the harmony changes four times per bar at quarter = 42, so the progression itself carries the melody.","Bar 2: a whole bar in Ab (VI) with Db (bII), the same chords that later set up the final cadence in bar 8.","Bars 5–7: the bass falls chromatically C–B–Bb–A–Ab–G, then F–Eb, under a nearly stepwise melody (lament bass).","Bar 6: French sixth Ab–C–D–F# opens out onto the G octave.","Beat-3 dotted rhythm with an appoggiatura (Eb→D, G→F, B→A) adds a sigh to most bars.","Bars 9–12 repeat 5–8 exactly; the contrast in editions is dynamic only."],"loop_candidates":[{"start_bar":5,"end_bar":8,"why":"Self-contained phrase ending on a PAC to C minor; bar 5 restarts on Cm, so the seam is a tonic-to-tonic join.","quarter_range":[16,32],"requires_audition":true},{"start_bar":1,"end_bar":4,"why":"Ends on V (G), which leads back to the Cm of bar 1.","quarter_range":[0,16],"requires_audition":true}],"hook_candidates":[{"start_bar":1,"end_bar":2,"why":"The recognisable opening chord march: i–iv7–V7–i, then Ab–Db–Eb7–Ab.","quarter_range":[0,8]},{"start_bar":5,"end_bar":6,"why":"High Eb5–D5–C5 line over the chromatic bass and the French sixth.","quarter_range":[16,24]},{"start_bar":7,"end_bar":8,"why":"Double cadence: V65→i, then Neapolitan → V7 → i.","quarter_range":[24,32]}],"kpop_uses":[{"where":"verse","why":"Bars 5–8 as a slow piano bed: one chord per beat, chromatic falling bass, and the melody moves little, leaving space for a vocal."},{"where":"chorus","why":"Bars 1–4 as a heavy ballad chorus progression (i–iv7–V7–i, VI–bII–V7/VI–VI) at half time with drums; ends on V for a turnaround."},{"where":"bridge","why":"Bars 6–8: French sixth and Neapolitan before V7–i give a dark pre-resolution moment."}],"review_flags":[{"bar":1,"reason":"Draft read bar 1 as one Cm chord and missed the per-beat harmony; every bar was relabelled per quarter."},{"bar":2,"reason":"Ab is tonicized for one bar (I–IV–V7–I in Ab), not modulated; kept key c with a modulation event marking the brief Ab region and Roman numerals relative to C minor."},{"bar":5,"reason":"Beat 3 (B–D–Ab + F# sixteenth) left as ?: incomplete viio7 without F. Same in bar 9."},{"bar":6,"reason":"Beat 1 (A–C–G) left as ?: passing sonority on the chromatic bass, no complete triad. Same in bar 10."},{"bar":6,"reason":"Beat 2 labelled A-7b5 as the enharmonic spelling of the French sixth Ab–C–D–F#."},{"bar":7,"reason":"Draft IAC in bar 7 kept (V65 → i, melody Eb); the draft had no PAC in bar 8, added (G7 root position → Cm, top voice C)."},{"bar":9,"reason":"Dynamics (ff, p, pp, crescendo) are printed in editions but absent from the constant-velocity MIDI; only the B′ section description mentions them."}],"schema_version":1,"bars":[{"bar":1,"start_quarter":0.0,"duration_quarters":4.0,"key":"c","chords":[{"beat":1,"symbol":"Cm","rn":"i","function":"tonic"},{"beat":2,"symbol":"Fm7","rn":"iv7","function":"Eb held over from beat 1"},{"beat":3,"symbol":"G7","rn":"V7","function":"Eb appoggiatura falls to D; F on the sixteenth"},{"beat":4,"sym